  "scope": "Public C++/Python typed enlargement commands capture requested distance/units, original/result area, source owner/descriptor/revisions, TCZ and X calibration. Complete native V1 records validate their original equation before binding or replacing it with an explicit rebind; predicted destination resource refusals cannot bypass original validation or invoke callbacks. Strict replay uses recorded geometry, preserving a fresh current Previous through native selection semantics. Explicit rebind captures destination geometry/calibration/position. Borrowed geometry estimation avoids constructing a bounding editor or raster during command admission. Core working estimates charge retained display/record/geometry, padded enlargement and preparation annotation/metadata copies; source pixels/history, caller-owned inputs, Python/desktop conversion, GUI retained state, opaque callbacks, allocator overhead and host publication copies are outside this bound. Frozen request/control/limits/source precede callbacks. Resolve/validate/replay/rebind/prepare now deliver one coarse progress pair, forwarding geometry checkpoints/stages once; callback exceptions/cancellation expose no result. Selection-only preparation guards all captured revisions including Display; camera/navigation changes after capture therefore refuse. Shared Expand/Shrink dialogs capture source before editing, consume independent persistent15-pixel/calibrated defaults, convert units with X spacing, show source units/anisotropy and clipping notices, preserve invalid text and disable Apply. Per-command edits do not overwrite defaults, intentionally differing from remembered last-use preferences. Direct grow/shrink aliases use the admitted native service on ordinary/scientific documents. Changed recording appends once after prepared publication; no-ops append nothing. Dedicated workflow captured Replay and explicit current-selection Rebind controls are provided; generic batch-program support remains open. Native sessions preserve records and IEEE words, with explicit rebind for reopened owners. Windows/Linux each pass317 new command/editor checks,35 existing settings checks and all7436 preceding installed IDs, totaling7788 with zero failures/errors/skips. The288 row/unit pairs consume144 unchanged actual ImageJ rows, not288 new reference identities. Six source types/policies cover recording/session/source-word preservation; ordinary aliases preserve shared storage/history without sample reads. Both hosts pass16 native groups, installed core-only SDK consumers and three standalone app probes. Actual creator-owned C++ ImGui input checks scalar/RGB/IEEE menu/dialog controls, unit conversion, warnings, incomplete draft, literal21-cell result, recording, Cancel and stale-source refusal. Python Editor API exercises the same compiled owner separately; new Python-launch/OS/OpenGL gesture acceptance is not claimed. First compilation exposed a resolver initializer-order error, corrected before qualifying. A preparation-script assertion caught a narrower edit count before that edit ran; no acceptance was claimed. Initial Windows smoke reached302 cases and caught six nested coarse callbacks instead of two; the geometry child now suppresses duplicate outer coarse/forwarded callbacks while keeping kernel cancellation/checkpoints/stages. The original executable/source/test failure preimages are retained or archived. Later both Python runs reached314 cases and found a test comparing Settings object identities; corrected to value dictionaries, without changing product behavior. Final317 includes additional original-validation priority, finish-exception and ordinary-alias assertions. Final source seals cover557 compiled inputs. Tested installs, SDK/native carriers, menu observations, reports and logs remain; disposable environments/duplicate prefixes, SDK builds, pytest/native fixtures and standalone raw roots were CRC/every-member-SHA archived before confined removal. Off-grid irregular retention, remembered last-use behavior, generic batch integration, large-ROI managed UI/cancellation, paired-launch gestures and complete platform/resource/editor/Fiji acceptance remain open. All99 original triples and historical accepted runs/Auto expectations are unchanged.",
